Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max77759: charge at 500 mA from Default USB sources

Local only (not for upstream). tcpm gives CURRENT_MAX=0 for a Default-Rp
source when the TCPC has no BC1.2, so the charger never turned its buck on
from a PC port.
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c	2026-10-07 19:04:09.978497362 -0500
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c	2026-10-07 19:04:09.990645971 -0500
@@ -619,6 +619,14 @@
 		goto err;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * tcpm reports 0 for a Default-USB-power source (plain PC port or
+	 * USB-A charger) when the TCPC has no BC1.2 detection, which would
+	 * leave the buck off. Fall back to the USB 2.0 default of 500 mA.
+	 */
+	if (online.intval && !current_limit.intval)
+		current_limit.intval = 500000;
+
 	if (online.intval && current_limit.intval) {
 		ret = set_input_current_limit(chg, current_limit.intval);
 		if (ret) {
